  "question": {
    "text": "When the gap between two identical concave thin lenses&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>cm</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> placed in contact is filled with certain liquid, the image of an object placed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from lens combination shifts away from the lens by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. If the refractive index of the liquid is <math><mi>μ</mi></math>, then write <math><mn>3</mn><mi>μ</mi></math> as your answer."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "In case (i) (without liquid)<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0108_24d85dc15037.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"height: 168px; width: 140px;\" /><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3.75</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math><br />When the gap is filled with liquid<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>'</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3.75</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1.25</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math><br />Here, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math><br />Hence, <math><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>"
  }
